{
  "title": "Word Break",
  "description": "Given a string `s` and a list of dictionary words `words`, decide whether `s` can be written as one or more dictionary words placed one after another with nothing left over.\n\nA dictionary word may be used as many times as you like. Return `true` if `s` can be built this way and `false` otherwise.\n\n### Constraints\n\n- `1 <= s.size() <= 300`\n- `1 <= words.size() <= 100`\n- `1 <= words[i].size() <= 20`\n- `s` and every word contain only lowercase English letters, and the words are all different.\n- Inputs are passed as function arguments and the answer is returned from the function. Do not read from standard input or print the result.\n",
  "reference": "bool word_break(string s, vector<string> words) {\n    int n = s.size();\n    vector<bool> ok(n + 1, false);\n    ok[0] = true;\n    for (int end = 1; end <= n; ++end) {\n        for (const string& word : words) {\n            int length = word.size();\n            if (length <= end && ok[end - length] && s.compare(end - length, length, word) == 0) {\n                ok[end] = true;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return ok[n];\n}\n",
  "template": "bool word_break(string s, vector<string> words) {\n    // Return whether s can be split into dictionary words.\n    return false;\n}\n",
  "tags": [
    "Strings",
    "Hash Tables",
    "Dynamic Programming"
  ],
  "examples": [
